  "plain": "After a craft is said to have crashed near Aztec, New Mexico, in 1948, there were two sets of photos, and the set the government took did not last, fading away to nothing. Scott Ramsey, a researcher of the Aztec crash, tells it, pointing back to the original story by a writer named Frank Scully. If true, it would help explain why no government pictures of the crash survive."
